    "body": "- [x] I, the PR author, have personally reviewed every line of this PR.\n\n# What does this PR do?\n\nMakes `test_cudnn_attention_backward_pads_small_local_head_count` independent of the GPU it runs on.\n\nThe test replaces the cuDNN DSA module with a fake, but `_run_sparse_attention_backward` still reads the real device capability to choose the query-head padding. Below SM90 that lookup raises `cudnn fused DSA requires SM90+ (Hopper or later), got SM89.`, so the test fails on an L40S even though no cuDNN kernel runs. The test now pins `_current_sm` to SM90, the same way `test_cudnn_flash_mla_sm100_uses_smallest_supported_head_padding` pins SM100. The expected shapes are the SM90 padding (8 heads padded to 64). SM100 also pads 8 heads to 64, so the test checks the same thing on Hopper and Blackwell as before.\n\n## Issue tracking\n\nLinked issue: Related to #8546 (found in the same sm_89 unit-test run).\n\n## Testing\n\n| | main | this PR |\n|---|---|---|\n| L40S (sm_89) | fails with the SM90+ error | not run |\n| GH200 (sm_90) | passes | passes |\n| GH200, device capability reported as (8, 9) during the test | fails with the same error as on the L40S | passes |\n\nFor the last row, `torch.cuda.get_device_capability` was patched to return (8, 9) for the duration of the test and `dsa_cudnn_kernels._device_sm` was cleared before and after.\n\n- The rest of `test_dsa_native_parity.py` on this branch, without the absorbed-MLA parity cases: 55 passed, 4 skipped, 1 failed. The failure, `test_cudnn_sparse_loss_reduces_attention_target_across_tp`, fails the same way on main (`all_reduce_calls` stays 0 when no process group is initialized) and is unrelated to this change.\n- black 26.3.0 and isort 5.13.2 report no changes; pylint and ruff were not run.\n\nThe test keeps its `flaky`/`flaky_in_dev` markers. The comment above them describes a real-kernel CUDA error, but this test only uses the fake backend, so it may be possible to re-enable it. I left that to you because I can't see the CI failure the comment refers to.\n\nEnvironment: GH200, torch 2.14.1+cu130, Transformer Engine 2.20.2+44f31bbe.\n\n",
